// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
// Filename:	Spotlight Array PCB 0.5.test
// Project:		VSC90,VSC90,VSC80,VSC800
// Author:      Foster & Freeman Ltd - Paul Evans
// Modified:    
//
// Description: Using the TE209 with relay and pickit, Tests the  Flood Array PCB LED's 
// * Steps 3 to 5 are steup for the test box itself*
// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

[0] force FAIL by default to avoid IMPORTANT message below.

#1: Enter operator initials and PCB serial number:
a. Enter operator intials.
b. Enter serial number into the box below.
IMPORTANT: Observe ESD precautions for handling ESD sensitive devices.  
//DISPLAY: lamptrayPCB1.jpg
CLICK_OK:

#2: Equipment Setup 1
a. Using TE159 connect the PSU to the Controller Test Box(TE209).
b. Connect the PC (via USB) to K5 on the Test box (TE209).
c. Connect the PC (via USB) to the TENMA Programmable PSU.
d. Connect the PC to the LED Test Box with Web Camera (TE086).
//DISPLAY: TE132.jpg
CLICK_OK:


#3: Equipment Setup 2
a. Connect the UUT to the VSC90 Controller Test Box(TE209).
b. Connect the Spotlight PCB to the PCB Fixture (TE217).
c. Place the UUT inside the LED Test Box with Web Camera (TE086).
d. Set the TENMA Programmable PSU power switch to on.
CLICK_OK:
EXE: OpenWinCam.bat
CONNECT: I2C
COMMAND: I2C OUT RA0 0 // TURN RELAY OFF
CONNECT: TENMAPSU
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #3: 

#4: Configure the PSU
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCP1
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCPSET1:500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:12.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:1.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET2:5.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET2:0.300
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:1
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH2:0

#4.1: Power on the test box.
COMMAND: I2C OUT RA0 1 //TURN RELAY ON
DELAY: 500
COMMAND: I2C OUT RA0 0 // TURN RELAY OFF
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned voltage is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.060 0.015 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
IF: //true result, current is good
GOTO: #4.2: 

IMPORTANT: This test has failed, check the power button has been pressed, power supply, USB connection and the ftdi chip.		
PASS_FAIL: #4.1:


#4.2: Connect to the test box
IF, ERROR on line 65, CONNECT_ VSC90 - Not available message is displayed
Click OK
DELAY: 7000 // GIVE TIME FOR THE pc AND NEW ftdi TO WAKE
CONNECT: VSC90 // test connection to the FDTI chip
IF_NOT: // wrong FTDI porgram
GOTO: #4.3: // reprogram the FTDI and PIC
GOTO: #4.6: // FTDI is correct now check the PIC is programmed correctly 


#4.3: program the FTDI 
EXE: ftdi_programmer_vsc90.exe

#4.3.1: program the PIC
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH2:1
EXE: VSC90FWself_powered.bat
DELAY: 2000
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH2:0
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:0
DELAY: 2000
GOTO: #4.4: // 

#4.3.2: program the PIC attempt 2 
DISCONNECT: VSC90
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH2:1
EXE: VSC90FWself_powered.bat
DELAY: 2000
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH2:0
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:0
DELAY: 2000


#4.4:  Press the I/O Power button and turn on the test box
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:1
COMMAND: I2C OUT RA0 1 //TURN RELAY ON
DELAY: 500
COMMAND: I2C OUT RA0 0 // TURN RELAY OFF
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned voltage is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.060 0.015 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 				
IF_NOT: 
GOTO: #4.4: // user didnt press the IO in time or there is fault 

#4.5: Attempt Connect again.
DELAY: 5000 // GIVE TIME FOR THE pc AND NEW ftdi TO WAKE
CONNECT: VSC90
IF_NOT: 
GOTO: #4: // GO BACK TO THE START

#4.6: PCB Program version check.
COMMAND: VSC90  TYPE // Connection to the PIC chip
READLINE: VSC90  TYPE
Returned product is = %TYPE%
[%TYPE% STR_EQ VSC90] // evaluates inside the [] and set true or false flag
IF:
GOTO: #5: // checks and programming complete goto the start of tests
ELSE: // PIC is not programmed correctly still
IMPORTANT: Cannot program the test box (PIC). Please check connections to the PIC Kit and PCB.
CLICK_OK:
GOTO: #4.3.2: // try programming the PIC again


#5: PCB communication check
COMMAND: VSC90 SPOTSHIFT 1 //. This allows the Spot PCB to be directly plugged into the control PCB 
COMMAND: VSC90 ENUM
READLINE: VSC90 ENUM 
Check the expected result is a match.
Expected result is = SPOT,TEMP,ZOOM,EEPROM,
Returned result is = %ENUM%
[%ENUM% STR_EQ SPOT,TEMP,ZOOM,EEPROM,]// evaluates inside the [] and set true or false flag
SUB: TestPassOrFail // sends the outcome to flag to the subroutine for evaluation

#6: Test the VIOLET LED
COMMAND: VSC90 VIOLET 1023
DELAY: 2500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.280 0.010 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail

#7: Test the BLUE LED
COMMAND: VSC90 BLUE 1023
DELAY: 2500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.270 0.010 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail

#8: Test the BLUEGREEN LED
COMMAND: VSC90 BLUEGREEN 1023
DELAY: 2500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.283 0.010 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail

#9: Test the CYAN LED
COMMAND: VSC90 CYAN 1023
DELAY: 2500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.273 0.010 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail

#10: Test the RED LED
COMMAND: VSC90 RED 1023
DELAY: 2500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.250 0.010 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail

#11: Test the GREEN LED
COMMAND: VSC90 GREEN 1023
DELAY: 2500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.280 0.010 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail

#12: Test the DEEPRED LED
COMMAND: VSC90 DEEPRED 1023
DELAY: 2500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.235 0.010 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail

#13: Test the AMBER LED
COMMAND: VSC90 AMBER 1023
DELAY: 2500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.265 0.010 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail

#13: Test the FARRED LED
COMMAND: VSC90 FARRED 1023
DELAY: 2500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.225 0.010 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail

#14: Test the WHITESPOT LED
COMMAND: VSC90 WHITESPOT 1023
DELAY: 2500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.270 0.010 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail

#15: Test's Complete
COMMAND: VSC90 off
IF: %FAILED% > 0
GOTO: #Failed:
ELSE: #Passed:


#Failed: a test failed
This PCB has failed to pass all Tests
Check the Log file for more details on the failed test(s).
IMPORTANT: This PCB has failed to pass all Tests
DISPLAY: test_failed.png
CLICK_OK:
GOTO: #QUIT:

#Passed: Test's Complete
a. All tests instructions have been completed and a log file created.
b. Click OK to finish and power OFF.
DISPLAY: AllTestsPassed.png
CLICK_OK:

#QUIT:
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
EXE: CloseWinCam.bat
// End of file
